The unit tests for this PR are failing in CI due to this:

```
RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded
 ❯ parseGenericTypes packages/mermaid/src/diagrams/common/common.ts:193:36
    191|     do {
    192|       cleanedText = newCleanedText;
    193|       newCleanedText = cleanedText.replace(/~([^\s:;]+)~/, '<$1>');
       |                                    ^
    194|     } while (newCleanedText != cleanedText);
  Snapshots  1 failed
```

See https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/actions/runs/5870194330/job/15916763487.

I feel like this should instead be:

```suggestion
  it('17c: should handle the direction statement with LR', () => {
```

since it's more similar to the `17a: should handle the direction statement with BT` tests rather than the `18: ...` tests.

But, IMO, I'm not a big fan of manually numbering tests (do we know why we manually number tests?). Would something like the following be better?

```js
describe("should handle direction statement with", () => {
  for (const direction of ["BT", "RL", "LR"]) {
    it(direction, () => {
      imgSnapshotTest(`
        classDiagram
          direction ${direction}
          class Student {
            -idCard : IdCard
          }
          class IdCard{
            -id : int
            -name : string
          }
          class Bike{
            -id : int
            -name : string
          }
          Student "1" --o "1" IdCard : carries
          Student "1" --o "1" Bike : rides
        `,
        { logLevel: 1, flowchart: { htmlLabels: false } }
      );
    });
  }
});
```

Can you add some [TSDoc](https://tsdoc.org/) comments for this new `ClassMember` type? They can be pretty basic, e.g. something like:

```ts
/**
 * Stores class diagram member variables/methods.
 */
export class ClassMember {
  /** ???? */ // is this a DOM ID, or global/class-unique ID?
  id!: string;

  /** visibility, `+` for public, `-` for private, etc. */
  visibility!: string;
```

Ideally, if I'm (or someone else) is browsing the `classRenderer-v2.ts` file, our code-editor should show these TSDoc comments, so we don't need to jump to this file to figure out what each param/method does.

Should we limit this type so it can only be two different values?

```suggestion
  memberType!: 'method' | 'attribute';
  visibility!: string;
  classifier!: string;
  parameters!: string;
  returnType!: string;

  constructor(input: string, memberType: 'method' | 'attribute') {
```

Should this be `cssStyle` or `member.cssStyle`?

```suggestion
  if (cssStyle !== '') {
    tSpan.attr('style', cssStyle);
  }
```
